  "title": "Kerala's Strong Opposition to Mining Amendment Bill",
  "summary": "Kerala Chief Minister V.D. Satheesan opposes the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Amendment Bill, citing its potential violation of federal principles and the threat to state sovereignty over land. He plans to communicate this opposition to the central government.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Kerala Chief Minister V.D. Satheesan opposes the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Amendment Bill.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bill seeks to take away the states' rights and ownership over land, as outlined in the 7th schedule of the Constitution.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The amendment bill was passed by the Lok Sabha on Wednesday.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
